From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Vetter <julian.vetter@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:35:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg/DxeCore: Only notify varstored of SB failures on
 x86

The add-xen-variable patch makes CoreLoadImageCommon() notify varstored
of Secure Boot failures. The notification is sent through
XenVariableLib's exec_command(), which uses IoWrite32() to an x86 I/O
port. AArch64 has no port I/O, so any AArch64 platform that links
DxeCore, such as ArmVirtXen, fails to build:

  XenVariableLib.h:136: undefined reference to `IoWrite32'

varstored only exists for x86 HVM guests anyway. Restrict
XenNotifySecureBootFailure() and its call site to IA32 and X64.

Signed-off-by: Julian Vetter <julian.vetter@vates.tech>

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Core/Dxe/Image/Image.c b/MdeModulePkg/Core/Dxe/Image/Image.c
index ea32e6236ef6..e5d321e4c01e 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Core/Dxe/Image/Image.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Core/Dxe/Image/Image.c
@@ -1091,6 +1091,7 @@ CoreUnloadAndCloseImage (
   CoreFreePool (Image);
 }
 
+#if defined (MDE_CPU_IA32) || defined (MDE_CPU_X64)
 STATIC
 EFI_STATUS
 XenNotifySecureBootFailure (
@@ -1118,6 +1119,7 @@ XenNotifySecureBootFailure (
 
   return status;
 }
+#endif
 
 /**
   Loads an EFI image into memory and returns a handle to the image.
@@ -1339,6 +1341,7 @@ CoreLoadImageCommon (
                                   );
   }
 
+#if defined (MDE_CPU_IA32) || defined (MDE_CPU_X64)
   if (SecurityStatus == EFI_SECURITY_VIOLATION || SecurityStatus == EFI_ACCESS_DENIED) {
     EFI_STATUS NotifyStatus = XenNotifySecureBootFailure ();
 
@@ -1346,6 +1349,7 @@ CoreLoadImageCommon (
       DEBUG ((DEBUG_INFO, "XenNotifySecureBootFailure failed: %r\n",
               NotifyStatus));
   }
+#endif
 
   //
   // Check Security Status.
